From 80acb24331b31d4636f097bc4af7d2f6f1f47bba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:06:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] lifecycle guard: keep stdin feeds through compound
 commands spanning lines

`_iter_segment_contexts` walked each logical line with a fresh `_LineWalk`, so a group or
compound command whose body spans lines lost its feed. Each of these ran a lifecycle `.py`
that `scan_gateway_lifecycle` never opened ((False, None)):

    {                          cat f.py | while read l; do
    cat f.py                   python3
    } | python3                done

    cat f.py | if true; then   (
    python3                    cat f.py
    fi                         ) | python3

Five whys: the feed was lost because the walk state (open groups, pending output) died at
each line end; it did because the walk was written per line (#2393) and only a trailing
pipe was joined (#2485); a newline is a command separator, not a script boundary, so a
group's `{`, body and `}` are one command list.

Fix: walk the whole command with one `_LineWalk`, a newline ending a command as `;` does
(`iter_script_segment_contexts`). A heredoc body is not part of that script: its `{`/`}`
line would open or close a group of the command around it (`{` / `cat <<EOF` / `}` /
`EOF` / `cat f.py` / `} | python3` then lost its feed). `heredoc_scripts` (on the new
`tools.shell_heredoc.heredoc_body_spans`) walks the command without its bodies, then each
body as a script of its own (`bash <<EOF` bodies are one; a multi-line group inside one is
now caught too). An unterminated or unparsable heredoc splits nothing from there on, so
that text stays in the main walk. A line shlex rejects still falls back to its physical
lines, which now join the same walk.

Proof:
- New tests/cron/test_lifecycle_guard_multiline_feed.py (lifecycle_guard.py is at 1979
  of its 2000-line cap): 32 must-scan cases, 17 must-stay-allowed cases and a
  heredoc_scripts contract. On the base (PR #2485 head 9bc067adf0) 33 of 50 fail: all
  32 must-scan cases plus the contract (no heredoc_scripts); everything passes here.
- 10 mutants of the new code: 9 killed; the survivor (heredoc_body_spans scanning past
  the last `<<`) only costs time.
- The 240 test files importing lifecycle_guard / shell_heredoc / terminal_tool pass:
  6461 passed, 40 skipped.
- Replayed 9365 distinct real terminal commands from worker-7's state.db (638
  multi-line) through scan_gateway_lifecycle, base vs head: 0 verdicts changed, 0 errors.
